      "writtenOn": "2023-08-07T13:30:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"This approach focuses on making the C++ code focus on decoding and drawing the image and moves the logic of deciding which combination of configuration options to Bazel. Instead of relying on many nested for loops with nested conditionals to determine what images to decode in which way to be drawn on which surfaces, we elected to go for a list comprehension of explicit options to make it more clear what is being tested. While (hopefully) reducing the complexity of the test harness, this should also be helpful in breaking up tests for better sharding.\"",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 177,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 187
      },
      "revId": "05bb85556e1d614a4d4f35735ff579b5bc0c3902",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
